# Read-only GitHub token, used on the server only (never sent to the browser).
# It powers the project list, open-source pull requests and the contribution graph.
# A fine-grained token with read access to public repositories is enough.
# Without it the site falls back to GitHub's unauthenticated REST list: repos and stars
# still load, but pinned repos, pull requests and the activity graph are not shown.
GITHUB_READ_TOKEN=

# GitHub account to read (defaults to Drix10).
#GITHUB_USERNAME=Drix10
